                                            <div class="card-group" style="text-align: left;padding: 8px;">
                                                <h3 style="font-weight:700;">Signs and symptoms:</h3>
                                                <div>
                                                    <p>
                                                        Symptoms usually begin 7 to 14 days after infection.
                                                        <br />
                                                        <i>Measles isn't just a little rash. Measles can be dangerous, especially for babies and young children.</i>
                                                        <br />
                                                        7–14 days after a measles infection: first symptoms show
                                                        Measles symptoms appear 7 to 14 days after contact with the virus. Measles typically begins with:
                                                    </p>

                                                    <p style="font-weight:700;">Initial Symptoms begin 7–14 days after a patient is infected with measles.</p>
                                                    <p>These are the first symptoms the patient may have:</p>
                                                    <ul>
                                                        <li>
                                                            High fever (may spike to more than 104°)
                                                        </li>
                                                        <li>Cough</li>
                                                        <li>Runny nose (coryza)</li>
                                                        <li>Red, watery eyes (conjunctivitis)</li>
                                                    </ul>


                                                    <p style="font-weight:700;">Symptoms:2–3 days after initial symptoms begin, Koplik spots may appear inside the mouth </p>
                                                    <ul>
                                                        <li>
                                                            Koplik spots
                                                        </li>
                                                        <li>
                                                            Tiny white spots (Koplik spots) may appear inside the mouth two to three days after symptoms begin
                                                        </li>
                                                    </ul>

                                                    <p style="font-weight:700;">Symptoms: Measles rash:</p>
                                                    <p>Occour 3–5 days after initial symptoms start. It usually begins as flat red spots that appear on the face at the hairline. They then spread downward to the neck, trunk, arms, legs, and feet.</p>
                                                    <br />
                                                    <ul>
                                                        <li>
                                                            Small raised bumps may also appear on top of the flat red spots.
                                                        </li>
                                                        <li>
                                                            The spots may become joined together as they spread from the head to the rest of the body.
                                                        </li>
                                                        <li>
                                                            When the rash appears, a person's fever may spike to more than 104° Fahrenheit.
                                                        </li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </div>

